diff --git a/evidence/03-independent-classification.txt b/evidence/03-independent-classification.txt
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..eed0e72b17462bf537310881d76b6566fd4112ff
--- /dev/null
+++ b/evidence/03-independent-classification.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+FROZEN SOURCES INSPECTED
+- /reference/k-proof/verification.k lines 1-48
+- /reference/k-proof/spec.k lines 1-173
+- /reference/k-proof/solution.py lines 1-11
+- /reference/k-proof/prove.sh lines 1-58
+- supplied semantics core.k lines 13-14 and 223-225
+- supplied semantics list.k lines 18-20, 24-25, and 53-55
+- supplied semantics subscript.k lines 11-14, 38-39, 64-65, and 109-114
+- supplied semantics int.k lines 15-20
+- supplied semantics sort.k lines 18-24 and 34-42
+
+INDEPENDENT CLASSIFICATION
+1. rule-ea80... (verification.k 11-12): DEFINITION. Base case for the fresh recursive summary mergeThirdFrom; it never matches an operational MPY configuration.
+2. rule-8eaaf... (14-17): DEFINITION. Recurrence for a remaining index divisible by three; it selects element I/3 of the sorted third-position sequence and advances I.
+3. rule-48604... (19-22): DEFINITION. Complementary recurrence for non-third positions; it selects source element I and advances I.
+4. rule-0855... (29-35): DEFINITION. Folding macro/named proof term connecting the complete mergeThirdFrom summary to fresh sortThirdResult; it does not preempt Python execution.
+5. rule-684be... (37-39): DOMAIN_LEMMA. It asserts the zero-length consequence for the named complete-result summary. Stage 1 compiles it into verification-kompiled before any proof and contains no earlier proof of the exact rule in a module omitting it, so it is not PROVED_DERIVED_LEMMA. It is relevant for the source contract's empty-list case and the final summary.
+6. rule-a119... (42-44): DOMAIN_LEMMA. Associativity of the existing valSeqConcat defined by .ValSeq-left identity and vCons recursion in supplied list.k. It is not a definition of a fresh summary and was not separately proved before use. It is relevant to re-associating the accumulated loop-output concatenation after each append.
+7. rule-d101... (47): DOMAIN_LEMMA. Right identity of that same left-recursive concatenation, again not separately proved. It is relevant when mergeThirdFrom reaches its empty base at loop exit.
+
+CONSISTENCY AND RELEVANCE
+- All four rules tagged simplification are classified only as DEFINITION or DOMAIN_LEMMA.
+- The two merge recurrence guards are exhaustive over I < N because pyMod(I,3) is an integer and equality versus disequality to zero are complementary; the I >= N base supplies termination.
+- valSeqConcat associativity and right identity are true by structural induction on the first ValSeq argument using supplied list.k lines 19-20.
+- vsLen is nonnegative on the algebraic ValSeq constructors by core.k lines 223-225, so the zero-length guard identifies the empty sequence; the complete merge definition then reduces by its base case.
+- No local rule is an ordinary K-cell execution/observation rule, so OPERATIONAL_RULE is empty.
+- prove.sh has only the loop invariant and final claims from spec.k, after compiling every verification.k rule; there is no bridge-free, earlier kprove of any exact local rule. PROVED_DERIVED_LEMMA is therefore empty.
+
+JUDGMENT
+The protected Stage 3 classifications match the independent classification exactly. The true domain-lemma set is nonempty and consists of precisely rules 5-7.
