+INTERPRETATION
+- The first three results match the frozen source on representative, identity-distinguishing, negative, and multi-chunk integer cases.
+- concat([1,2],[3,4]) = [1,2,3,4], vsLen([-1,0,1]) = 3, -2 <= 1 is true, and 2 <= 1 is false.
+- Inspection of the exact definitions confirms: _<=Int_ is Lean integer <=; concat is structural recursion matching list.k 19-20; vsLen is structural recursion matching core.k 223-225; the integer branch of sortThirdResult selects indices 0,3,6,..., stably sorts them, and merges them back at those indices, matching solution.py and verification.k 11-35.
+
+COUNTERFACTUAL MUTATION
+Counterfactual.lean, created only in the audit copy, defines operationally correct <=, vsLen, and concat but deliberately defines sortThirdResult as identity. It then proves the unchanged generated target.
