+SortVal.«setV(_)_MPY-SET_Val_IntSeq» : SortIntSeq → SortVal
+SortVal.«typeV(_)_MPY-CORE_Val_String» : SortString → SortVal
+
+There is no SortStr type, no str(IntSeq) constructor in SortIterable, and no string-value injection into SortVal. SortString occurs only as metadata/name arguments of unrelated constructors, not as the K string value constructor. Consequently no generated SortValSeq can represent the frozen K term vCons(str(...), ...).
+
+JUDGMENT
+The target's universal VS/A/B/C quantifiers range over this strictly smaller generated SortValSeq. The string-containing cases covered by the frozen ValSeq sort and the supplied `sortVS` operational equations are absent. This is a mathematical weakening of every universally quantified ValSeq obligation, despite exact hashes and an exact source-rule record bijection. The candidate's sortThirdResult cannot implement the frozen string sorting branch because its input type has no such values. This is both a Stage 4 fixed-target/domain failure and an operational-bridge failure under the user's explicit criteria.

